  q: "A 35-year-old female presents to the ER with a fever, confusion, and a petechial rash. Labs show a hemoglobin of 7.2 g/dL, platelets of 15,000/µL, BUN 45 mg/dL, and Creatinine 2.8 mg/dL. Peripheral smear shows numerous schistocytes. PT and aPTT are perfectly normal. What is the primary pathophysiological mechanism of her disorder?",
