  exp: "The pentad of Fever, Anemia (Microangiopathic Hemolytic Anemia with schistocytes), Thrombocytopenia, Renal failure, and Neurologic symptoms ('FAT RN') is classic for Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura (TTP). TTP is caused by a severe deficiency of ADAMTS13 (usually due to an acquired autoantibody). ADAMTS13 is a metalloproteinase that cleaves ultra-large von Willebrand Factor (vWF) multimers. Without it, uncleaved vWF multimers tether platelets in the microcirculation, causing microthrombi and shearing RBCs (schistocytes). The coagulation cascade is not activated, so PT and aPTT are NORMAL.",
