  q: "A 16-year-old girl is brought to the ER after intentionally ingesting an unknown amount of acetaminophen (paracetamol) 12 hours ago. She currently complains of nausea and right upper quadrant abdominal pain. Laboratory tests show AST and ALT over 5,000 U/L. Which of the following toxic metabolites is responsible for this massive hepatocellular necrosis, and what is the specific antidote?",
